# Engineering Forge - Documentation Rules

## 🎯 DOCUMENTATION OVERVIEW
You are working on the documentation system for "Engineering Forge". This directory contains all project documentation organized using Domain-Driven Design (DDD) principles.

## 🚨 CRITICAL DOCUMENTATION RULES

### RULE 1: ALWAYS MAINTAIN CONSISTENCY
- ALWAYS follow the established documentation structure
- ALWAYS use consistent formatting and styling
- ALWAYS maintain cross-references between documents
- ALWAYS keep the PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md updated

### RULE 2: ALWAYS UPDATE RELATED DOCUMENTS
- When updating a domain document, ALWAYS update the main domain README
- When updating a version document, ALWAYS update the main version README
- When updating specifications, ALWAYS update related technical docs
- When updating business docs, ALWAYS update related business docs

### RULE 3: ALWAYS USE TEMPLATES
- ALWAYS use the templates in `TEMPLATES/document-templates/`
- ALWAYS follow the established document structure
- ALWAYS include all required sections
- ALWAYS maintain template consistency

### RULE 4: ALWAYS VERIFY LINKS
- ALWAYS check that all internal links work
- ALWAYS verify external links are accessible
- ALWAYS maintain proper link formatting
- ALWAYS update broken links immediately

### RULE 5: ALWAYS FOLLOW DDD STRUCTURE
- ALWAYS work within the defined domain boundaries
- ALWAYS update domain-specific documentation
- ALWAYS maintain domain separation
- ALWAYS respect domain responsibilities

## 📁 DOCUMENTATION STRUCTURE

```
docs/
├── README.md                           # Main entry point
├── PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md               # Central progress tracking
├── PROJECT-OVERVIEW.md                 # Project overview
├── CURSOR-SYSTEM.md                    # Cursor methodology
├── CURSOR-RULES.md                     # Cursor rules
├── CURSOR-METHODOLOGY.md               # Work methodology
├── CURSOR-COMMANDS.md                  # Standardized commands
├── CURSOR-CHAT-TEMPLATE.md             # Chat template
├── DOMAINS/                            # DDD domains
│   ├── education/                      # Education domain
│   ├── gaming/                         # Gaming domain
│   ├── blockchain/                     # Blockchain domain
│   ├── user-management/                # User management domain
│   ├── marketplace/                    # Marketplace domain
│   ├── analytics/                      # Analytics domain
│   └── README.md                       # Domain overview
├── VERSIONS/                           # Product versions
│   ├── v1.0-prototype/                 # V1.0 prototype
│   ├── v2.0-mvp-web/                   # V2.0 MVP web
│   ├── v3.0-3d-web/                    # V3.0 3D web
│   ├── v4.0-vr/                        # V4.0 VR
│   └── README.md                       # Version overview
├── DEVELOPMENT/                        # Development process
│   ├── architecture/                   # System architecture
│   ├── implementation/                 # Implementation guides
│   ├── tasks/                          # Task management
│   └── testing/                        # Testing strategies
├── SPECIFICATIONS/                     # Technical specifications
│   ├── game-design/                    # Game design specs
│   ├── technical-design/               # Technical design specs
│   ├── ui-ux/                          # UI/UX specifications
│   └── api-design.md                   # API specifications
├── BUSINESS/                           # Business aspects
│   ├── monetization/                   # Monetization strategies
│   ├── market-analysis/                # Market analysis
│   ├── go-to-market/                   # Go-to-market strategy
│   └── business-plans/                 # Business plans
├── GUIDES/                             # User and developer guides
│   ├── getting-started/                # Getting started guides
│   ├── developer-guides/               # Developer documentation
│   ├── user-guides/                    # User documentation
│   └── maintenance/                    # Maintenance guides
├── TEMPLATES/                          # Document templates
│   ├── document-templates/             # Documentation templates
│   ├── code-templates/                 # Code templates
│   └── report-templates/               # Report templates
├── ASSETS/                             # Visual resources
│   ├── diagrams/                       # System diagrams
│   ├── mockups/                        # UI mockups
│   ├── prototypes/                     # Prototypes
│   └── media/                          # Media files
└── archive/                            # Archived documents
    ├── deprecated/                     # Deprecated documents
    ├── old-versions/                   # Old versions
    ├── reports/                        # Historical reports
    └── temp/                           # Temporary files
```

## 📝 DOCUMENTATION STANDARDS

### Formatting Standards
- Use Markdown (.md) for all documentation
- Follow consistent heading hierarchy (H1 > H2 > H3)
- Use proper markdown syntax and formatting
- Include table of contents for long documents
- Use consistent emoji and icon usage

### Content Standards
- Write clear, concise, and professional content
- Use active voice and present tense
- Include examples and code snippets where appropriate
- Maintain consistent terminology across all documents
- Include relevant links and cross-references

### Structure Standards
- Always include a title and overview section
- Use consistent section naming and organization
- Include status indicators and metadata
- Add proper navigation and breadcrumbs
- Include relevant links and references

## 🔄 DOCUMENTATION WORKFLOW

### Creating New Documents
1. Choose appropriate template from `TEMPLATES/document-templates/`
2. Follow template structure and requirements
3. Include all required sections and metadata
4. Add proper cross-references and links
5. Update related documents and indexes

### Updating Existing Documents
1. Read current document thoroughly
2. Make changes while maintaining consistency
3. Update related documents and cross-references
4. Update PROGRESS-DASHBOARD.md if needed
5. Verify all links still work

### Archiving Documents
1. Move outdated documents to `archive/`
2. Update any references to archived documents
3. Maintain archive organization and structure
4. Update navigation and indexes

## 🎯 DOMAIN-SPECIFIC RULES

### Education Domain
- Focus on learning objectives and outcomes
- Include assessment and evaluation criteria
- Maintain educational best practices
- Update curriculum and course materials

### Gaming Domain
- Focus on game mechanics and player experience
- Include gameplay loops and progression systems
- Maintain game design principles
- Update game balance and mechanics

### Blockchain Domain
- Focus on security and decentralization
- Include smart contract specifications
- Maintain blockchain best practices
- Update integration and wallet features

### User Management Domain
- Focus on security and user experience
- Include authentication and authorization
- Maintain privacy and data protection
- Update user profiles and preferences

### Marketplace Domain
- Focus on commerce and trading
- Include pricing and payment systems
- Maintain marketplace best practices
- Update product catalogs and transactions

### Analytics Domain
- Focus on data collection and insights
- Include metrics and reporting systems
- Maintain analytics best practices
- Update dashboards and reports

## 🚀 QUALITY ASSURANCE

### Review Process
- All documents must be reviewed before publication
- Check for accuracy, completeness, and consistency
- Verify all links and references work
- Ensure proper formatting and structure

### Maintenance Process
- Regularly review and update documentation
- Check for outdated information and links
- Maintain consistency across all documents
- Archive obsolete documents appropriately

### Standards Compliance
- Follow established documentation standards
- Maintain consistent formatting and style
- Use proper templates and structures
- Include all required metadata and information

